{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:98522","published":"2026-11-12T00:04:12.119552Z","modified":"2026-11-12T00:30:03.620223025Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-102276","CVE-2026-102278","CVE-2026-105482","CVE-2026-105483","CVE-2026-106069","CVE-2026-109383","CVE-2026-109829","CVE-2026-109869","CVE-2026-111497","CVE-2026-87018"],"summary":"Important: nodejs:26 security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"Node.js is a software development platform for building fast and scalable network applications in the JavaScript programming language. \n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via uncontrolled recursion in nested brace patterns (CVE-2026-102278)\n\n* brace-expansion: brace-expansion: Denial of Service via stack exhaustion from crafted brace patterns (CVE-2026-102276)\n\n* undici: undici: Denial of Service via unhandled stream error on excessive content encodings (CVE-2026-109869)\n\n* undici: undici: Denial of Service via TLS renegotiation with mismatched certificate (CVE-2026-87018)\n\n* undici: undici: Certificate validation bypass via dropped TLS options in Agent (CVE-2026-109383)\n\n* undici: undici: Cache poisoning and information disclosure via improper cross-origin redirect caching (CVE-2026-109829)\n\n* brotli: Out-of-Bounds Write in Google Brotli Decoder (CVE-2026-111497)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: TLS certificate hostname bypass via fullwidth-digit IP hostnames (CVE-2026-105483)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: TLS certificate hostname bypass via non-canonical IP hostnames (CVE-2026-106069)\n\n* nodejs: nodejs: dns.resolve truncates hostnames containing a NUL character (CVE-2026-105482)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* nodejs:26/nodejs: Rebase to the latest Node.js 26 release [rhel-9.9] (JIRA:Rocky Linux-289767)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":